Before you buy new headphones, watch this.
Most wireless earbuds have their batteries glued in. When the battery fades, you can't replace it, so the whole pair goes in the bin.
Now multiply that by every device we own. In 2022 the world threw away a record 62 million tonnes of electronics. That's enough to fill 1.55 million trucks, lined up bumper to bumper around the equator. Less than a quarter of it was properly recycled. And India is now the third-largest e-waste generator on the planet.
It doesn't have to be that way. A few brands are actively making tech you can keep instead of replace:
@TheHouseofMarley : Bamboo, FSC-certified wood, recycled aluminium, and fabric spun from recycled materials.
@marshall Major V: 86% recycled plastic, replaceable ear cushions, and over 100 hours of playtime.
@Fairphone  Fairbuds XL: You can swap out the battery and ear cushions yourself. Fix the part, keep the pair.
@M_Aiaiai  TMA-2: Fully modular. The headband, earpads, cable and speakers are all separate, so you replace only what wears out.
@gomidesign  : A speaker handmade in Brighton from waste plastic and batteries rescued from old e-bikes, with lifetime repairs.
Save this for your next upgrade, and send it to the friend who goes through a pair of earbuds every year.

#techinnovation #techgadgets #sustainability #innovation
